                        "review": "[h2][b]It looks boring but actually isn't [/b][/h2]\n[quote][b] Rating: 8/10 [/b][/quote]\n\nIf you are not into investigation genre like me, I think this is a good one to begin with. And don't worry, you will never get stuck because all the cases are very well curated. There are 26 crimes to solve in a post World War II setting of Los Angeles, California in year 1947. \n\n[h3]What is the gameplay like?[/h3][list]\n[*] You are a cop, don't expect reckless action in the open world.\n[*] Investigation involves finding clues in a given scene, interrogating people, and identifying if they are lying or telling truth using your logic, clues, and their body language/expression.\n[*] Fair bit of action too - shooting, street chases, and car chases. Most of the action is in side activities but plenty in main ones too.\n[*] You always work in pairs as detectives. Hence, you can skip most of the driving part if you want.\n[/list]\n\n[h3]Who can I recommend this game to?[/h3][list]\n[*] Dexter & Mafia DE fans.\n[*] Those who want to feel the authority as they walk down the old American streets with three-piece suit and the iconic hat. Enhanced with great music.\n[/list]\n\n[h3]Negatives?[/h3][list]\n[*] Understanding every detail in dialogue requires a very good proficiency in English. I was struggling from time to time. Too many names and places got me confused too.\n[*] I'm not technically sure I'm right, but sometimes I had multiple clues to back my statement against a person.. but game forces to select a particular clue to succeed.\n[*] While every case is well made with enough variety, it kind of gets stale somewhere in between. Same loop of - slowly going over the dead body, driving the slow vehicle from your station to the scene, chasing suspects, etc.\n[*] Don't expect much depth in the story of protagonist. I found the ending to be disappointing too.\n[*] 30 FPS lock. External frame gen tool like LSFG recommended if you don't want to break driving physics with mod.\n[/list]\n\n[h3][b]Overall, a solid slow-paced detective game with a mix of action in between which isn't really hard to complete.[/b][/h3]",
